            "bug_id": 19278,
            "text": "Created attachment 4006\npatch: parenthesize negative constants in needsparens() (v2)\n\nUpdated patch attached; it supersedes attachment 3997. Following review on the GitHub PR, it adds a comment explaining why the integer branch has to exclude NA_INTEGER (it is INT_MIN, so it would otherwise pass the < 0 test, whereas NA_real_ and NaN already compare false) and extends the regression test to check that NA_integer_^2 and NA_real_^2 still deparse unchanged. The fix itself is the same. Generated against r90833, applies cleanly to r90836.\n\nPatch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/452",
